course: dictionary
lesson: 9534
title: Learning a word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name animals or things you may never have seen. «In cold northern places a stoat's coat turns white in winter, keeping only the black tail tip; this white fur is called ermine.» The words around ermine tell you what it is: a white winter coat with a black tail tip.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. Here "this white fur" points back to ermine, so ermine must be another name for that fur. Check by swapping in your meaning: "this white fur is called white winter fur" still makes sense, so your guess fits.
explain: Stoat is a noun, a word for a thing or animal. In «The stoats were in a flap, running all ways», the stoats are the ones doing the running. Ask who or what is doing the action, and you have found the noun.
fact: A stoat is a small, fierce, meat-eating animal.
fact: A stoat has a long thin body, short legs, brown fur and a black tip on its tail.
fact: In cold places a stoat's fur turns white in winter, except for the black tail tip.
fact: This white winter fur is called ermine, and it was once used on kings' robes.
fact: In New Zealand stoats were brought in and became pests that kill native birds like kiwi.
exercise: «In cold northern places a stoat's coat turns white in winter, keeping only the black tail tip.» What is this white winter fur called? | Skua | *Ermine | Sentry | Lemming
exercise: «Snowy owls, Arctic foxes, stoats and skuas depend on lemmings.» What do the stoats depend on? | Trifle | Snow | Badger | *Lemmings
exercise: «The stoats were in a flap, running all ways.» What does "in a flap" suggest? | Fast asleep | Eating a big supper | *Worried and rushing about | Very calm and quiet
test: «Mole goes out to check on the stoat sentries.» What is a sentry? | A cold chicken | A stoat's baby | A kind of tree | *A guard who keeps watch
test: In winter, which part of a stoat stays black, even when its fur turns white? | Its eyes | Its nose | *Its tail tip | Its legs
exam: What is a stoat? | A sort of cold chicken served at supper | *A small, fierce, meat-eating animal with a long thin body | A large bird that catches fish | A kind of white fur used on robes
